- Scope: close the invoked `RemotingCommand` custom-header and ext-field helper
  slice on the Phase 18 branch. The Phase 18 plan was not modified.

## Changes

- `RemotingCommand` now owns an optional typed custom header and a typed decoded
  header cache. Rust borrows expose attached values; `write_custom_header(None)`
  clears the attachment. Explicit materialization and both wire codecs merge
  non-null header fields with existing ext-fields, preserving Java overwrite
  behavior while leaving the Rust command map unchanged during immutable encode.
- Added `add_ext_field` and `add_ext_field_if_not_exist`. The latter returns a
  typed `ProtocolError` if no map exists; pinned Java dereferences null and
  throws `NullPointerException` on that input.
- Java fixture invokes attach/read identity, post-attach mutation, null clear,
  cached/direct decode, ext-field helper and null-map behavior. Rust differential
  checks the fixture, both codec outputs and cached-reference reuse.
- Remaining representation difference: Rust transfers an owned typed header
  and requires the `CommandHeader` trait rather than retaining arbitrary Java
  object aliases and using reflection. Cached and attached references remain
  mutable through Rust borrows. This slice does not close the broader P18-V01
  audit.

